        "paragraphs": [
          "Learning rate is the size of a training adjustment. An epoch is one complete pass through the training examples; a batch is one smaller group within that pass. Connect this recipe to Train\u2019s scheduler input and connect an explicit optimizer recipe too. The scheduler changes training adjustments, not the model\u2019s forward connections.",
          "Move adjustment size between two fractions of the starting rate. Inspect the rate used for each completed update and the next rate separately. Constructor initialization happens before training and is not counted as a completed schedule tick.",
          "OneCycle advances after each successful batch; the other schedules advance after a complete pass and its validation results. A validation result measures the model on examples held out from training. ReduceLROnPlateau watches the selected result; its improvement direction is explicit and never guessed from that selection.",
          "A planned OneCycle horizon fixes the total number of batches. A cosine schedule stops at its reviewed minimum endpoint. The displayed final OneCycle next rate can be an unused terminal value; no training update may use it after the horizon is exhausted.",
          "An exact CPU checkpoint continues the same optimizer and schedule memory. Fine-tuning reuses model settings but starts fresh optimizer and schedule memory. Private lessons measure actual rates, learned adjustments and timing; a correct-looking name does not pass by itself."
